IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- PART 8 -- Information, Investigation and Directions (regulations 65 to 74C of the Money
-- Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer)
-- Regulations 2017, S.I. 2017/692, United Kingdom), lines 2200-2447 of uksi-2017-692.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A decision function answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.
-- JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (a definition that "means", a condition
-- introduced by "if", "only if" or "unless", a flat negative); each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (...)` with the quoted words.  NOTHING is "the text does not answer": it lists
-- without closing the list, says "includes", leaves a term undefined, is silent, points
-- outside the sources, or limits a grant or a duty in its own wording and the case falls
-- outside the limit; each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.  A caller must never
-- turn NOTHING into FALSE.  Marginal readings, listed in NOTES.md: (a) a failed "if" or an
-- "is"-definition and a flat negative are the text's no; (b) a grant or a prohibition limited
-- by its own wording is not a no; (c) a "must" that has not been done is the text's no.
-- Rulings of 2026-11-05, tagged `[ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]` and `[ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]`
-- on the branch (they are not the marginal readings above): a period the text fixes in its own
-- words answers JUST FALSE outside it; a "where" condition that is not met answers JUST FALSE;
-- a scope limit with no "only" answers NOTHING outside the scope.
-- A duty function (a "must") answers JUST FALSE only for a breach.  Where the duty arises "if" or
-- "where" something holds, a companion function, `... the duty ... arises`, answers JUST FALSE when
-- it does not arise, and the duty function answers NOTHING then.
-- A seam is marked `-- SEAM S-n (asking|answering)`.

§ `Part 8 -- Information, Investigation and Directions`

§§ `Regulation 65 -- Interpretation`

-- src:2202 | (1) In this Part—
-- src:2203 | “premises” means any building or other structure, including a moveable structure, other than premises used only as a dwelling;
-- src:2204 | “tribunal” means the First-tier Tribunal or, where determined by or under Tribunal Procedure Rules, the Upper Tribunal;
@ref reg 65(1) (src:2202-2204)
DECLARE `reg 65(1) tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `reg 65(1) the First-tier Tribunal`
    `reg 65(1) the Upper Tribunal`

-- Reg 65(1) "premises": "means" closes the definition, so a thing that is not a building or other structure, or that is used only as a dwelling, is not premises.
@ref reg 65(1) "premises" (src:2203)
GIVEN `it is a building or other structure, including a moveable structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used only as a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(1) the place is premises` IS
    IF NOT `it is a building or other structure, including a moveable structure`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“premises” means any building or other structure, including a moveable structure"
    ELSE IF `it is used only as a dwelling`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than premises used only as a dwelling"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Reg 65(1) "tribunal": the First-tier Tribunal or, where determined by or under Tribunal Procedure Rules, the Upper Tribunal.  The definition is total, so the answer is never "not covered".
@ref reg 65(1) "tribunal" (src:2204)
GIVEN `the Upper Tribunal is determined by or under Tribunal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 65(1) tribunal`
DECIDE `reg 65(1) the tribunal for the purposes of Part 8 is` IS
    IF `the Upper Tribunal is determined by or under Tribunal Procedure Rules`
    THEN `reg 65(1) the Upper Tribunal`
    ELSE `reg 65(1) the First-tier Tribunal`

-- Reg 65(2): who is an "officer" and who is a "relevant officer" in Part 8.  The rendering prints the four limbs of "officer" without their letters, and the line "a relevant officer;" (2210) follows an "or" at line 2208: fork F-OFFICER reads it as the fourth limb.
-- src:2205 | (2) Unless otherwise defined in this Part—
-- src:2206 | “officer” means—
-- src:2207 | an officer of the FCA, including a member of the FCA's staff or an agent of the FCA;
-- src:2208 | an officer of Revenue and Customs; or
-- src:2209 | an employee or agent of a professional body listed in Schedule 1 who is authorised by the body to act on behalf of the body for the purposes of this Part;
-- src:2210 | a relevant officer;
-- src:2211 | “relevant officer” means—
-- src:2212 | in Great Britain, an officer of a local weights and measures authority;
-- src:2213 | in Northern Ireland, an officer of the Department for the Economy,
-- src:2214 | acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners for the purposes of these Regulations.
@ref reg 65(2) (src:2205-2214)
DECLARE `reg 65(2) person` HAS
    `an officer of the FCA, including a member of the FCA's staff or an agent of the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an officer of Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employee or agent of a professional body listed in Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by that body to act on behalf of the body for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an officer of a local weights and measures authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an officer of the Department for the Economy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `where the person acts` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
    `acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 65(2) "relevant officer" (src:2211-2214)
GIVEN p IS A `reg 65(2) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(2) the person is a relevant officer` IS
    IF     p's `acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners`
       AND (   (    (p's `where the person acts` EQUALS `England and Wales` OR p's `where the person acts` EQUALS Scotland)
                AND p's `an officer of a local weights and measures authority`)
            OR (    p's `where the person acts` EQUALS `Northern Ireland`
                AND p's `an officer of the Department for the Economy`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant officer” means— in Great Britain, an officer of a local weights and measures authority; in Northern Ireland, an officer of the Department for the Economy, acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners"

@ref reg 65(2) "officer" (src:2206-2210)
GIVEN p IS A `reg 65(2) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(2) the person is an officer` IS
    IF     p's `an officer of the FCA, including a member of the FCA's staff or an agent of the FCA`
        OR p's `an officer of Revenue and Customs`
        OR (    p's `an employee or agent of a professional body listed in Schedule 1`
            AND p's `authorised by that body to act on behalf of the body for the purposes of this Part`)
        OR `reg 65(2) the person is a relevant officer` p EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“officer” means—"

-- Reg 65(3): a connected person is one listed in Schedule 5 in relation to the relevant person or payment service provider.  Schedule 5 belongs to part mlr5, so its answer is an input.
-- src:2215 | (3) For the purposes of this Part, a person is connected to a relevant person or a payment service provider (“a connected person”) if that person is a person listed in Schedule 5 in relation to the relevant person or payment service provider.
@ref reg 65(3) (src:2215)
-- SEAM S-16 (asking)
GIVEN `sch 5 the person is a connected person of the relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(3) the person is a connected person` IS
    CONSIDER `sch 5 the person is a connected person of the relevant person`
    WHEN JUST listed THEN
        IF listed
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that person is a person listed in Schedule 5" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 5 has not answered

§§ `Regulation 66 -- Power to require information`

-- Reg 66(1): a supervisory authority may, by notice in writing, require P (a person who is or was at any time a relevant person, a payment service provider or a connected person) to provide information, produce documents or attend and answer questions.
-- src:2217 | (1) A supervisory authority may, by notice in writing to a person (“P”) who is (or was at any time) a relevant person, a payment service provider or a connected person, require P to—
-- src:2218 | (a) provide specified information, or information of a specified description;
-- src:2219 | (b) produce specified documents, or documents of a specified description; or
-- src:2220 | (c) attend before an officer of the supervisory authority (or of a supervisory authority which is acting on behalf of that authority) at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions.
@ref reg 66(1) (src:2217-2220)
DECLARE `reg 66(1) what the notice requires` IS ONE OF
    `reg 66(1)(a) the notice requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description`
    `reg 66(1)(b) the notice requires P to produce specified documents, or documents of a specified description`
    `reg 66(1)(c) the notice requires P to attend before an officer at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions`

-- "A supervisory authority" is a body that reg 7(1) makes one.  Reg 7 is the keel's; its answer for the relevant person arrives as the list below.  A body not on the list is not shown to be one: the text of reg 66 does not say it is not (NOTHING).
@ref reg 66(1) "A supervisory authority" (src:2217)
-- SEAM S-K3 (asking)
GIVEN body IS AN Authority
      `reg 7(1) the supervisory authorities of the relevant person` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF Authority)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(1) the body is a supervisory authority` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 7(1) the supervisory authorities of the relevant person`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 7 has not answered
    WHEN JUST authorities THEN
        IF elem body authorities
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a body that regulation 7(1) does not list for this relevant person may be a supervisory authority for another

-- Reg 66(1): the grant.  It reaches P only if P is, or was at any time, a relevant person, a payment service provider or a connected person; it is exercised by notice in writing; limb (c) needs a time and place specified in the notice.
@ref reg 66(1) (src:2217-2220)
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 66(1) the body is a supervisory authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 65(3) the person is a connected person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the notice requires` IS A `reg 66(1) what the notice requires`
      `a time and place are specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(1) the supervisory authority may require P` IS
    IF `reg 66(1) the body is a supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF     `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `the person is a payment service provider`
            OR `reg 65(3) the person is a connected person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN IF `the notice is in writing`
              THEN IF     `what the notice requires` EQUALS `reg 66(1)(c) the notice requires P to attend before an officer at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions`
                      AND (NOT `a time and place are specified in the notice`)
                   THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at a time and place specified in the notice"
                   ELSE JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by notice in writing"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is (or was at any time) a relevant person, a payment service provider or a connected person"; also the case where the regulation 8 and Schedule 5 answers are not in
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a supervisory authority is not shown

-- Reg 66(1A): the power in paragraph (1) "includes" the power to require a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure made to the NCA.  "Includes" does not close the list.
-- src:2221 | (1A) The power in paragraph (1) includes power to require P to provide a copy of any suspicious activity disclosure made to the NCA.
@ref reg 66(1A) (src:2221)
GIVEN `the information required is a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure made to the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(1A) the power in paragraph (1) includes requiring the information` IS
    IF `the information required is a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure made to the NCA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes)

-- Reg 66(2): the information or documents must be provided or produced before the end of such reasonable period, and at such place, as may be specified.  A period is counted in days from the notice; an act on the last day of the period is before its end.  If the notice specifies no period, or a period that is not a reasonable one, the text does not say when (NOTHING).
-- src:2222 | (2) The information or documents must be provided or produced—
-- src:2223 | (a) before the end of such reasonable period as may be specified; and
-- src:2224 | (b) at such place as may be specified.
@ref reg 66(2) (src:2222-2224)
GIVEN `the period specified in the notice, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the period specified is a reasonable one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the information or documents were provided or produced, counting the day of the notice as day 0` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(2)(a) the information or documents were provided or produced in time` IS
    CONSIDER `the period specified in the notice, in days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the notice specified no period
    WHEN JUST days THEN
        IF NOT `the period specified is a reasonable one`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such reasonable period as may be specified"
        ELSE IF `the day on which the information or documents were provided or produced, counting the day of the notice as day 0` AT MOST days
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of such reasonable period as may be specified" [marginal (c)]

@ref reg 66(2)(b) (src:2224)
GIVEN `they were provided or produced at the place specified in the notice` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(2)(b) the information or documents were provided or produced at the specified place` IS
    CONSIDER `they were provided or produced at the place specified in the notice`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the notice specified no place
    WHEN JUST atPlace THEN
        IF atPlace
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at such place as may be specified" [marginal (c)]

-- The duty in reg 66(2)(a) as a regulative rule: P must provide or produce within the period the notice specifies.  A trace prints its outcome and cannot be asserted on the main binary; the decision function above carries the assertions.
DECLARE `reg 66(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 66(2) P`

DECLARE `reg 66(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 66(2) P provides the information or produces the documents`

@ref reg 66(2)(a) (src:2223)
GIVEN `the period specified in the notice, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 66(2) party` `reg 66(2) action`
DECIDE `reg 66(2)(a) P must provide the information or produce the documents` IS
    PARTY `reg 66(2) P`
    MUST `reg 66(2) P provides the information or produces the documents`
    WITHIN `the period specified in the notice, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 66(2) P` BECAUSE "the information or documents were not provided or produced before the end of the period specified in the notice"

-- Reg 66(3): an officer with written authorisation from a supervisory authority may require P, without unreasonable delay, to provide specified information or produce specified documents.  Limb (c) of paragraph (1), attendance, is not among the two limbs: the list does not say it is excluded (NOTHING).  The function consults reg 66(4), which says the powers "may only be exercised" by a supervisory authority or an officer authorised under paragraph (3), and only for information or documents reasonably required: an officer with no authorisation in writing, or a requirement that is not reasonably required, answers JUST FALSE (66(4) is an "only", marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2225 | (3) An officer who has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so may require P without unreasonable delay to—
-- src:2226 | (a) provide the officer with specified information or information of a specified description; or
-- src:2227 | (b) produce to the officer specified documents or documents of a specified description.
@ref reg 66(3) (src:2225-2227)
DECLARE `reg 66(3) what the officer requires` IS ONE OF
    `reg 66(3)(a) the officer requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description`
    `reg 66(3)(b) the officer requires P to produce specified documents, or documents of a specified description`
    `reg 66(3) the officer requires something else of P`

-- src:2225 | (3) An officer who has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so may require P without unreasonable delay to—
-- src:2226 | (a) provide the officer with specified information or information of a specified description; or
-- src:2227 | (b) produce to the officer specified documents or documents of a specified description.
-- src:2228 | (4) The powers in this regulation may only be exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority, in relation to information or documents which are reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of its supervisory functions.
@ref reg 66(3) and 66(4) (src:2225-2227) (src:2228)
GIVEN `reg 65(2) the person is an officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 66(4) the powers in regulation 66 may be exercised` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the officer requires` IS A `reg 66(3) what the officer requires`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(3) the officer may require P` IS
    IF `reg 65(2) the person is an officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the officer has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so`
         THEN CONSIDER `reg 66(4) the powers in regulation 66 may be exercised`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The powers in this regulation may only be exercised ... in relation to information or documents which are reasonably required" [marginal (a)]
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                  CONSIDER `what the officer requires`
                  WHEN `reg 66(3)(a) the officer requires P to provide specified information, or information of a specified description` THEN JUST TRUE
                  WHEN `reg 66(3)(b) the officer requires P to produce specified documents, or documents of a specified description` THEN JUST TRUE
                  WHEN `reg 66(3) the officer requires something else of P` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (3) names two requirements and does not say others are barred
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): reg 66(4) has not been answered for this requirement
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The powers in this regulation may only be exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is not shown

@ref reg 66(3) "without unreasonable delay" (src:2225)
GIVEN `the officer required P under paragraph (3) to provide information or produce documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P did so without unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(3) P provided or produced without unreasonable delay` IS
    IF `the officer required P under paragraph (3) to provide information or produce documents`
    THEN IF `P did so without unreasonable delay`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without unreasonable delay" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for a requirement made under paragraph (3)

-- Reg 66(4): the powers "may only be exercised" by a supervisory authority, or an officer authorised under paragraph (3), in relation to information or documents reasonably required in connection with its supervisory functions.  "Supervisory function" is a reg 3(1) term (the keel); whether the need is "reasonable" is a judgment the text hands to the authority, taken here as a plain input.
-- src:2228 | (4) The powers in this regulation may only be exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority, in relation to information or documents which are reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of its supervisory functions.
@ref reg 66(4) (src:2228)
GIVEN `they are exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or documents are reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of its supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(4) the powers in regulation 66 may be exercised` IS
    IF `they are exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority` AND `the information or documents are reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of its supervisory functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority, in relation to information or documents which are reasonably required" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 66(5): the notice must set out the reasons why the information is required or the documents produced, unless the authority or officer is not permitted to disclose them.  The paragraph speaks of information and documents, not of attendance: "Where ... requires information to be provided or documents to be produced under paragraph (1) or (3)" is the condition under which the duty arises, so the companion function answers JUST FALSE for a notice that requires attendance only (ruled 2026-11-05, (b)), and the function below, whose JUST FALSE means a breach, answers NOTHING there.
-- src:2229 | (5) Where a supervisory authority or an officer requires information to be provided or documents to be produced under paragraph (1) or (3), the notice must set out the reasons why the information is required to be provided or the documents produced, unless the supervisory authority or (as the case may be) the officer is not permitted to disclose this information.
@ref reg 66(5) (src:2229)
GIVEN `what the notice requires` IS A `reg 66(1) what the notice requires`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(5) the duty to set out the reasons arises` IS
    IF `what the notice requires` EQUALS `reg 66(1)(c) the notice requires P to attend before an officer at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a supervisory authority or an officer requires information to be provided or documents to be produced under paragraph (1) or (3)" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 66(5) (src:2229)
GIVEN `what the notice requires` IS A `reg 66(1) what the notice requires`
      `the notice sets out the reasons why the information is required to be provided or the documents produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority or the officer is not permitted to disclose this information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(5) the notice complies with the requirement to set out the reasons` IS
    IF `what the notice requires` EQUALS `reg 66(1)(c) the notice requires P to attend before an officer at a time and place specified in the notice and answer questions`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (5) speaks of information to be provided and documents to be produced, not of attendance; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 66(5) the duty to set out the reasons arises`
    ELSE IF     `the notice sets out the reasons why the information is required to be provided or the documents produced`
            OR `the supervisory authority or the officer is not permitted to disclose this information`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice must set out the reasons why the information is required to be provided or the documents produced, unless" [marginal (c)]

-- Reg 66(6): two further powers of the supervisory authority, over the form of what it receives.
-- src:2230 | (6) The supervisory authority may require—
-- src:2231 | (a) information contained in a computer or other storage device, or recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form to be produced to it in legible form or in a form from which the information can readily be produced in visible and legible form; and
-- src:2232 | (b) any information provided under this regulation to be provided in such form as it may reasonably require.
@ref reg 66(6) (src:2230-2232)
GIVEN `the information is contained in a computer or other storage device, or recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be produced in legible form or in a form from which it can readily be produced in visible and legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(6)(a) the supervisory authority may require the information to be produced in legible form` IS
    IF `the information is contained in a computer or other storage device, or recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form` AND `it is to be produced in legible form or in a form from which it can readily be produced in visible and legible form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information contained in a computer or other storage device, or recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form"

@ref reg 66(6)(b) (src:2232)
GIVEN `the information was provided under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is one the supervisory authority may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(6)(b) the supervisory authority may require the information to be provided in the form` IS
    IF `the information was provided under this regulation` AND `the form is one the supervisory authority may reasonably require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any information provided under this regulation"; whether a form is one it may "reasonably require" is the authority's judgment, taken as an input

-- Reg 66(7): producing a document does not affect a lien.
-- src:2233 | (7) The production of a document does not affect any lien which a person has on the document.
@ref reg 66(7) (src:2233)
GIVEN `the document is produced under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(7) the production of the document affects a lien on it` IS
    IF `the document is produced under this regulation`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect any lien which a person has on the document" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of production under this regulation

-- Reg 66(8): the power can be exercised in relation to a third person who holds the document.  "If ... it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person" is the condition; outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2234 | (8) If a supervisory authority has power under this regulation to require a person to produce a document but it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person, that power may be exercised by the supervisory authority in relation to the third person.
@ref reg 66(8) (src:2234)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority has power under this regulation to require a person to produce a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(8) the supervisory authority may exercise the power in relation to the third person` IS
    IF `the supervisory authority has power under this regulation to require a person to produce a document` AND `it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a supervisory authority has power under this regulation to require a person to produce a document but it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person, that power may be exercised by requiring the third person to produce the document" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 66(9): "suspicious activity disclosure" is given its meaning by regulation 104(4); the definition is that row (part 11), and this function is the pointer, as the keel's pointers are.
-- src:2235 | (9) In this regulation, “suspicious activity disclosure” has the meaning given in regulation 104(4).
@ref reg 66(9) (src:2235)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 66(9) suspicious activity disclosure is given by` MEANS "regulation 104(4)"

§§ `Regulation 67 -- Requests in support of other authorities`

-- Reg 67(1): on a request to which paragraph (2) applies the supervisory authority may exercise the reg 66 power, and reg 66 is read as if it also referred to information and documents reasonably required to meet the request.
-- src:2237 | (1) On receiving a request to which paragraph (2) applies from a foreign authority, the supervisory authority may exercise the power conferred by regulation 66, and for these purposes, regulation 66 has effect as if it also referred to information and documents reasonably required by the supervisory authority to meet such a request.
@ref reg 67(1) (src:2237)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority has received a request from a foreign authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 67(2) paragraph (2) applies to the request` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 67(1) the supervisory authority may exercise the power in regulation 66 to meet the request` IS
    IF `the supervisory authority has received a request from a foreign authority` AND (`reg 67(2) paragraph (2) applies to the request` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On receiving a request to which paragraph (2) applies from a foreign authority"

-- Reg 67(2): which requests paragraph (2) reaches.  The text introduces the list with "applies if", so a request made for none of the three purposes is outside it (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2238 | (2) This paragraph applies if the request is made by the foreign authority in connection with the exercise by that authority of—
-- src:2239 | (a) functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive;
-- src:2240 | (b) functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation; or
-- src:2241 | (c) functions provided for in the law of a third country equivalent to those provided for in the fourth money laundering directive or the funds transfer regulation.
@ref reg 67(2) (src:2238-2241)
GIVEN `the request is made in connection with the exercise by the foreign authority of functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made in connection with the exercise by the foreign authority of functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made in connection with the exercise by the foreign authority of functions provided for in the law of a third country equivalent to those provided for in the fourth money laundering directive or the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 67(2) paragraph (2) applies to the request` IS
    IF `the request is made in connection with the exercise by the foreign authority of functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive` OR `the request is made in connection with the exercise by the foreign authority of functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation` OR `the request is made in connection with the exercise by the foreign authority of functions provided for in the law of a third country equivalent to those provided for in the fourth money laundering directive or the funds transfer regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies if the request is made by the foreign authority in connection with the exercise by that authority of—" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 67(3): matters the supervisory authority may take into account "in particular": the list is not closed.
-- src:2242 | (3) In deciding whether or not to exercise its powers under regulation 66 in response to a request, the supervisory authority may take into account in particular—
-- src:2243 | (a) whether, in the territory of the foreign authority concerned, corresponding assistance would be given to the supervisory authority;
-- src:2244 | (b) whether the case concerns the breach of a law, or other requirement, which has no close parallel in the United Kingdom or involves the assertion of a jurisdiction not recognised by the United Kingdom;
-- src:2245 | (c) the seriousness of the case and its importance to persons in the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 67(3) (src:2242-2245)
DECLARE `reg 67(3) matter` IS ONE OF
    `reg 67(3)(a) whether, in the territory of the foreign authority concerned, corresponding assistance would be given to the supervisory authority`
    `reg 67(3)(b) whether the case concerns the breach of a law, or other requirement, which has no close parallel in the United Kingdom or involves the assertion of a jurisdiction not recognised by the United Kingdom`
    `reg 67(3)(c) the seriousness of the case and its importance to persons in the United Kingdom`
    `reg 67(3) some other matter`

@ref reg 67(3) (src:2242-2245)
GIVEN matter IS A `reg 67(3) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 67(3) the supervisory authority may take the matter into account` IS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `reg 67(3)(a) whether, in the territory of the foreign authority concerned, corresponding assistance would be given to the supervisory authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 67(3)(b) whether the case concerns the breach of a law, or other requirement, which has no close parallel in the United Kingdom or involves the assertion of a jurisdiction not recognised by the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 67(3)(c) the seriousness of the case and its importance to persons in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 67(3) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may take into account in particular"

-- Reg 67(4): the authority may decide not to exercise its powers unless the foreign authority undertakes both things.
-- src:2246 | (4) The supervisory authority may decide not to exercise its powers under regulation 66 unless the foreign authority undertakes—
-- src:2247 | (a) to make such contribution towards the cost of doing so as the supervisory authority considers appropriate; and
-- src:2248 | (b) to comply with such conditions in relation to the information and documents as the supervisory authority considers appropriate.
@ref reg 67(4) (src:2246-2248)
GIVEN `the foreign authority undertakes to make such contribution towards the cost as the supervisory authority considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign authority undertakes to comply with such conditions in relation to the information and documents as the supervisory authority considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 67(4) the supervisory authority may decide not to exercise its powers` IS
    IF     `the foreign authority undertakes to make such contribution towards the cost as the supervisory authority considers appropriate`
       AND `the foreign authority undertakes to comply with such conditions in relation to the information and documents as the supervisory authority considers appropriate`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the foreign authority undertakes" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Reg 67(6): "foreign authority".
-- src:2250 | (6) “Foreign authority” means an authority in a territory which is not part of the United Kingdom which exercises functions referred to in paragraph (2).
@ref reg 67(6) (src:2250)
GIVEN `it is an authority in a territory which is not part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it exercises functions referred to in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 67(6) the authority is a foreign authority` IS
    IF `it is an authority in a territory which is not part of the United Kingdom` AND `it exercises functions referred to in paragraph (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Foreign authority” means an authority in a territory which is not part of the United Kingdom which exercises functions referred to in paragraph (2)"

-- The two together (hand-gathered, ruling E1 option B as guidance): the reach of the reg 66 powers is reg 66(4) as extended by reg 67(1).  Reg 66(4) and reg 67(1) each keep their own function.
-- src:2228 | (4) The powers in this regulation may only be exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority, in relation to information or documents which are reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of its supervisory functions.
-- src:2237 | (1) On receiving a request to which paragraph (2) applies from a foreign authority, the supervisory authority may exercise the power conferred by regulation 66, and for these purposes, regulation 66 has effect as if it also referred to information and documents reasonably required by the supervisory authority to meet such a request.
@ref reg 66(4) and 67(1) (src:2228) (src:2237)
GIVEN `they are required by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of its supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are reasonably required by the supervisory authority to meet a request to which regulation 67(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(4) and 67(1) the information or documents may be required under regulation 66` IS
    IF `they are required by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority` AND (`they are reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of its supervisory functions` OR `they are reasonably required by the supervisory authority to meet a request to which regulation 67(2) applies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be exercised by a supervisory authority, or by an officer authorised under paragraph (3) to act on behalf of the supervisory authority, in relation to information or documents which are reasonably required" [marginal (a)]

§§ `Regulation 68 -- Requests to other authorities`

-- Reg 68(1): when the regulation applies.  "Applies if": a case with any limb missing is outside it (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2252 | (1) This regulation applies if—
-- src:2253 | (a) documents or information which are reasonably required by a supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by the authority of any of the functions given to it under these Regulations are not (as far as the supervisory authority is aware) available in the United Kingdom; and
-- src:2254 | (b) the supervisory authority has reason to believe that such documents or information may be held by a person who is within the jurisdiction of a foreign authority.
@ref reg 68(1) (src:2252-2254)
GIVEN `documents or information are reasonably required by a supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by it of any of the functions given to it under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are not (as far as the supervisory authority is aware) available in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has reason to believe that they may be held by a person who is within the jurisdiction of a foreign authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 68(1) this regulation applies` IS
    IF `documents or information are reasonably required by a supervisory authority in connection with the exercise by it of any of the functions given to it under these Regulations` AND `they are not (as far as the supervisory authority is aware) available in the United Kingdom` AND `the supervisory authority has reason to believe that they may be held by a person who is within the jurisdiction of a foreign authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies if—" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 68(2): the supervisory authority may request the foreign authority's assistance in obtaining information or documents which satisfy the conditions in paragraph (1).  Paragraph (1) says "This regulation applies if", so it governs paragraph (2) too: a request outside the conditions answers JUST FALSE, and an answer that reg 68(1) has not given leaves NOTHING.
-- src:2255 | (2) A supervisory authority may request the assistance of the foreign authority in obtaining specified information or documents which satisfy the conditions in paragraph (1).
@ref reg 68(2) (src:2255)
GIVEN `reg 66(1) the body is a supervisory authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 68(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 68(2) the supervisory authority may request the assistance of the foreign authority` IS
    IF (`reg 66(1) the body is a supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN IF (`reg 68(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF (NOT (`reg 68(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies if" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A supervisory authority may request": who may ask is a scope limit with no "only" (ruled 2026-11-05, (c)); "information or documents which satisfy the conditions in paragraph (1)" is the condition, and paragraph (1) says "applies if", so a case outside reg 68(1) answers JUST FALSE

-- Reg 68(3) and (4): what the information may be used for, and the foreign authority's consent.
-- src:2256 | (3) The information or documents provided to the supervisory authority pursuant to a request under paragraph (2) must only be used—
-- src:2257 | (a) for the purpose for which it was provided; or
-- src:2258 | (b) for the purposes of proceedings arising as a result of contravention of a relevant requirement in these Regulations, or proceedings arising out of such proceedings.
@ref reg 68(3) (src:2256-2258)
GIVEN `the information or documents were provided to the supervisory authority pursuant to a request under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are used for the purpose for which they were provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are used for the purposes of proceedings arising as a result of contravention of a relevant requirement in these Regulations, or proceedings arising out of such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 68(3) the use made of the information or documents is permitted` IS
    IF `the information or documents were provided to the supervisory authority pursuant to a request under paragraph (2)`
    THEN IF `they are used for the purpose for which they were provided` OR `they are used for the purposes of proceedings arising as a result of contravention of a relevant requirement in these Regulations, or proceedings arising out of such proceedings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must only be used" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The information or documents provided to the supervisory authority pursuant to a request under paragraph (2)"

-- src:2259 | (4) Paragraph (3) does not apply if the foreign authority by which the information or documents were provided consents to its use.
@ref reg 68(4) (src:2259)
GIVEN `the foreign authority by which the information or documents were provided consents to its use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 68(4) paragraph (3) applies` IS
    IF `the foreign authority by which the information or documents were provided consents to its use`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (3) does not apply if the foreign authority by which the information or documents were provided consents to its use" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says when paragraph (3) does not apply and nothing of when it does

-- Reg 68(5): "foreign authority" has the meaning given in regulation 67(6): a pointer.
-- src:2260 | (5) In this regulation, “foreign authority” has the meaning given in regulation 67(6).
@ref reg 68(5) (src:2260)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 68(5) foreign authority is given by` MEANS "regulation 67(6)"

-- SEAM S-12 (answering): reg 60 (part mlr3) asks whether a person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66.  The answer is a fact built from the facts of the four ways to fail: after the period, at the wrong place, not attending or not answering, or delaying a requirement made by an officer.
-- src:2222 | (2) The information or documents must be provided or produced—
-- src:2223 | (a) before the end of such reasonable period as may be specified; and
-- src:2224 | (b) at such place as may be specified.
-- src:2225 | (3) An officer who has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so may require P without unreasonable delay to—
-- src:2226 | (a) provide the officer with specified information or information of a specified description; or
-- src:2227 | (b) produce to the officer specified documents or documents of a specified description.
@ref reg 66 (failure to comply, S-12) (src:2222-2227)
-- SEAM S-12 (answering)
GIVEN `P did not provide the information or produce the documents before the end of the period specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P did not provide the information or produce the documents at the place specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice required P to attend and P did not attend or did not answer questions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P delayed unreasonably in doing what an officer required under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66` IS
        `P did not provide the information or produce the documents before the end of the period specified in the notice`
    OR  `P did not provide the information or produce the documents at the place specified in the notice`
    OR  `the notice required P to attend and P did not attend or did not answer questions`
    OR  `P delayed unreasonably in doing what an officer required under paragraph (3)`

§§ `Regulation 69 -- Entry, inspection of premises without a warrant etc`

-- Reg 69(4): "duly authorised officer" means an FCA officer authorised in writing by a Head of Department in the FCA's enforcement function, or a Revenue and Customs officer authorised in writing by an officer of at least the grade of senior officer.
-- src:2276 | (4) In this regulation, “duly authorised officer” means—
-- src:2277 | (a) an officer of the FCA, authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation on behalf of the FCA or another supervisory authority, by a Head of Department working within the enforcement function of the FCA; or
-- src:2278 | (b) an officer of Revenue and Customs authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation on behalf of the Commissioners, or another supervisory authority, by an officer of Revenue and Customs of at least the grade of senior officer.
@ref reg 69(4) (src:2276-2278)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation on behalf of the FCA or another supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is by a Head of Department working within the enforcement function of the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation on behalf of the Commissioners, or another supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is by an officer of Revenue and Customs of at least the grade of senior officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 69(4) the person is a duly authorised officer` IS
    IF (`the person is an officer of the FCA` AND `the person is authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation on behalf of the FCA or another supervisory authority` AND `the authorisation is by a Head of Department working within the enforcement function of the FCA`) OR (`the person is an officer of Revenue and Customs` AND `the person is authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation on behalf of the Commissioners, or another supervisory authority` AND `the authorisation is by an officer of Revenue and Customs of at least the grade of senior officer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“duly authorised officer” means"

-- Reg 69(1): paragraph (2) applies where a duly authorised officer of (or acting on behalf of) a supervisory authority in relation to a relevant person or payment service provider has reasonable grounds to believe the two things.  Limb (b)(i) is blank in this text (line 2265).  "Applies where": the whole of the where clause is the condition, so a case with any limb of it missing is outside the paragraph and the answer is JUST FALSE (ruled 2026-11-05, (b)); an answer that another provision gives and that is not in leaves NOTHING (fork F-69-1).
-- src:2262 | (1) Paragraph (2) applies where a duly authorised officer of (or acting on behalf of) a supervisory authority in relation to a relevant person or a payment service provider (“P”) has reasonable grounds to believe that—
-- src:2263 | (a) any premises are being used by P in connection with P's business or professional activities; and
-- src:2264 | (b) P may have contravened the requirements of—
-- src:2265 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2266 | (ii) the funds transfer regulation, or
-- src:2267 | (iii) these Regulations.
@ref reg 69(1) (src:2262-2267)
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 69(4) the person is a duly authorised officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer is of, or is acting on behalf of, a supervisory authority in relation to P` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `P is a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that any premises are being used by P in connection with P's business or professional activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that P may have contravened the requirements of the funds transfer regulation or of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS
    IF (`reg 69(4) the person is a duly authorised officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the officer is of, or is acting on behalf of, a supervisory authority in relation to P` AND ((`reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `P is a payment service provider`) AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that any premises are being used by P in connection with P's business or professional activities` AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that P may have contravened the requirements of the funds transfer regulation or of these Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT (`reg 69(4) the person is a duly authorised officer` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND `the officer is of, or is acting on behalf of, a supervisory authority in relation to P` AND ((NOT (`reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR `P is a payment service provider`) AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that any premises are being used by P in connection with P's business or professional activities` AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that P may have contravened the requirements of the funds transfer regulation or of these Regulations`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies where a duly authorised officer of (or acting on behalf of) a supervisory authority in relation to a relevant person or a payment service provider (“P”) has reasonable grounds to believe that" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]

-- Reg 69(2): what the officer may do, on producing evidence of authority, at any reasonable time.  The six powers are listed without "only", so a seventh is not covered either way.
-- src:2268 | (2) The officer may, on producing evidence of the officer's authority, at any reasonable time—
-- src:2269 | (a) enter the premises;
-- src:2270 | (b) inspect the premises;
-- src:2271 | (c) observe the carrying on of business or professional activities by P;
-- src:2272 | (d) inspect any documents or other information found on the premises;
-- src:2273 | (e) require any person on the premises to provide an explanation of any document or to state where documents or information might be found;
-- src:2274 | (f) inspect any cash found on the premises.
@ref reg 69(2) (src:2268-2274)
DECLARE `reg 69(2) power` IS ONE OF
    `reg 69(2)(a) enter the premises`
    `reg 69(2)(b) inspect the premises`
    `reg 69(2)(c) observe the carrying on of business or professional activities by P`
    `reg 69(2)(d) inspect any documents or other information found on the premises`
    `reg 69(2)(e) require any person on the premises to provide an explanation of any document or to state where documents or information might be found`
    `reg 69(2)(f) inspect any cash found on the premises`
    `reg 69(2) some other power`

@ref reg 69(2) (src:2268-2274)
GIVEN `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer produces evidence of the officer's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer acts at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `reg 69(2) power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 69(2) the officer may` IS
    IF `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the officer produces evidence of the officer's authority` AND `the officer acts at a reasonable time`
         THEN CONSIDER power
              WHEN `reg 69(2)(a) enter the premises` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reg 69(2)(b) inspect the premises` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reg 69(2)(c) observe the carrying on of business or professional activities by P` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reg 69(2)(d) inspect any documents or other information found on the premises` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reg 69(2)(e) require any person on the premises to provide an explanation of any document or to state where documents or information might be found` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reg 69(2)(f) inspect any cash found on the premises` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `reg 69(2) some other power` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the six powers are listed and the paragraph does not say others are barred
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on producing evidence of the officer's authority, at any reasonable time"
    ELSE IF `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies where a duly authorised officer of (or acting on behalf of) a supervisory authority in relation to a relevant person or a payment service provider (“P”) has reasonable grounds to believe that" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): reg 69(1) has not been answered

-- Reg 69(3): copies and extracts.
-- src:2275 | (3) The officer may take copies of, or make extracts from, any documents found as a result of the exercise of the power in paragraph (2).
@ref reg 69(3) (src:2275)
GIVEN `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the documents were found as a result of the exercise of the power in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 69(3) the officer may take copies of, or make extracts from, the documents` IS
    IF `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies where a duly authorised officer of (or acting on behalf of) a supervisory authority in relation to a relevant person or a payment service provider (“P”) has reasonable grounds to believe that" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
    ELSE IF `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN IF `the documents were found as a result of the exercise of the power in paragraph (2)`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any documents found as a result of the exercise of the power in paragraph (2)": documents found some other way are outside the paragraph (scope, ruling (c))
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): reg 69(1) has not been answered

§§ `Regulation 70 -- Entry of premises under warrant`

-- Reg 70(13): the three defined terms.  "Justice" is a different office in each part of the United Kingdom.
-- src:2325 | (13) In this regulation—
-- src:2326 | “duly authorised officer” means—
-- src:2327 | where a warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA or another supervisory authority, an officer of the FCA authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation by a Head of Department working within the enforcement function of the FCA,
-- src:2328 | where a warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the Commissioners or another supervisory authority, an officer of Revenue and Customs authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation by an officer of Revenue and Customs of at least the grade of senior officer;
-- src:2329 | “executing officer” means—
-- src:2330 | where a warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA, or of a supervisory authority for which the FCA is acting, a constable,
-- src:2331 | where a warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the Commissioners, or of a supervisory authority for which the Commissioners are acting, an officer of Revenue and Customs;
-- src:2332 | “justice” means—
-- src:2333 | in England and Wales, a justice of the peace;
-- src:2334 | in Northern Ireland, a lay magistrate; or
-- src:2335 | in Scotland, a sheriff or summary sheriff.
@ref reg 70(13) (src:2325-2335)
@ref reg 70(13) "justice" (src:2332-2335)
GIVEN `where the warrant is sought` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the person is a justice of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a lay magistrate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a sheriff or a summary sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(13) the person is a justice` IS
    IF     (`where the warrant is sought` EQUALS `England and Wales` AND `the person is a justice of the peace`)
        OR (`where the warrant is sought` EQUALS `Northern Ireland` AND `the person is a lay magistrate`)
        OR (`where the warrant is sought` EQUALS Scotland AND `the person is a sheriff or a summary sheriff`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“justice” means— in England and Wales, a justice of the peace; in Northern Ireland, a lay magistrate; or in Scotland, a sheriff or summary sheriff"

@ref reg 70(13) "duly authorised officer" (src:2326-2328)
GIVEN `the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA or another supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the FCA authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation by a Head of Department working within the enforcement function of the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the Commissioners or another supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of Revenue and Customs authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation by an officer of Revenue and Customs of at least the grade of senior officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(13) the person is a duly authorised officer` IS
    IF (`the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA or another supervisory authority` AND `the person is an officer of the FCA authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation by a Head of Department working within the enforcement function of the FCA`) OR (`the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the Commissioners or another supervisory authority` AND `the person is an officer of Revenue and Customs authorised in writing to exercise the powers under this regulation by an officer of Revenue and Customs of at least the grade of senior officer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“duly authorised officer” means— where a warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA or another supervisory authority"

@ref reg 70(13) "executing officer" (src:2329-2331)
GIVEN `the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA, or of a supervisory authority for which the FCA is acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the Commissioners, or of a supervisory authority for which the Commissioners are acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(13) the person is an executing officer` IS
    IF (`the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA, or of a supervisory authority for which the FCA is acting` AND `the person is a constable`) OR (`the warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the Commissioners, or of a supervisory authority for which the Commissioners are acting` AND `the person is an officer of Revenue and Customs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“executing officer” means— where a warrant is issued on the basis of information given on behalf of the FCA"

-- Reg 70(1): the justice may issue a warrant if satisfied, on oath, by a duly authorised officer acting for a supervisory authority, that there are reasonable grounds for believing the first, second or third set of conditions is satisfied or for suspecting that the fourth is.  Whether the person is a justice and whether the informant is a duly authorised officer are answers of reg 70(13); an answer not in is not a "no".
-- src:2280 | (1) A justice may issue a warrant under this regulation if satisfied on information given on oath (or in Scotland by evidence on oath) by a duly authorised officer acting on behalf of a supervisory authority that—
-- src:2281 | (a) there are reasonable grounds for believing that the first, second, or third set of conditions is satisfied; or
-- src:2282 | (b) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the fourth set of conditions is satisfied.
@ref reg 70(1) (src:2280-2282)
GIVEN `reg 70(13) the person is a justice` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied on information given on oath (or in Scotland by evidence on oath)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 70(13) the information is given by a duly authorised officer acting on behalf of a supervisory authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the first, second or third set of conditions is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the fourth set of conditions is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(1) the justice may issue a warrant` IS
    IF `reg 70(13) the person is a justice` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a justice is not shown
    ELSE IF `reg 70(13) the information is given by a duly authorised officer acting on behalf of a supervisory authority` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the informant is a duly authorised officer is not shown
         ELSE IF     (`reg 70(13) the person is a justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                 AND `the justice is satisfied on information given on oath (or in Scotland by evidence on oath)`
                 AND (`reg 70(13) the information is given by a duly authorised officer acting on behalf of a supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                 AND (   `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the first, second or third set of conditions is satisfied`
                      OR `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the fourth set of conditions is satisfied`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A justice may issue a warrant under this regulation if satisfied on information given on oath" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 70(2): what the application must state.
-- src:2283 | (2) The application for the warrant must—
-- src:2284 | (a) identify the premises to which the application relates and state that the premises is not used only as a dwelling;
-- src:2285 | (b) state that the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect a warrant is necessary in connection with the exercise of the supervisory functions of the supervisory authority for which the officer is acting and the warrant is sought for the purpose of those functions;
-- src:2286 | (c) state that the officer executing the warrant—
-- src:2287 | (i) will give to any person on the premises, when entering the premises, evidence of identification and authority to act on behalf of the supervisory authority, and
-- src:2288 | (ii) will give to that person, no later than on entering the premises, a notice identifying and explaining the powers exercisable under this regulation, and
-- src:2289 | (d) state that the warrant is sought in relation to material specified in the application, or that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there is material falling within regulation 66 on the premises.
@ref reg 70(2) (src:2283-2289)
GIVEN `an application for a warrant is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies the premises and states that the premises is not used only as a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect a warrant is necessary in connection with the exercise of the supervisory functions of the supervisory authority for which the officer is acting and that the warrant is sought for the purpose of those functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer executing the warrant will give to any person on the premises, when entering the premises, evidence of identification and authority to act on behalf of the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the officer executing the warrant will give to that person, no later than on entering the premises, a notice identifying and explaining the powers exercisable under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the warrant is sought in relation to material specified in the application, or that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there is material falling within regulation 66 on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(2) the application meets the requirements` IS
    IF `an application for a warrant is made`
    THEN IF `it identifies the premises and states that the premises is not used only as a dwelling` AND `it states that the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect a warrant is necessary in connection with the exercise of the supervisory functions of the supervisory authority for which the officer is acting and that the warrant is sought for the purpose of those functions` AND `it states that the officer executing the warrant will give to any person on the premises, when entering the premises, evidence of identification and authority to act on behalf of the supervisory authority` AND `it states that the officer executing the warrant will give to that person, no later than on entering the premises, a notice identifying and explaining the powers exercisable under this regulation` AND `it states that the warrant is sought in relation to material specified in the application, or that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there is material falling within regulation 66 on the premises`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application for the warrant must—" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The application for the warrant"

-- Reg 70(3) to (6): the four sets of conditions.  Each "is" definition is read as closed (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2290 | (3) The first set of conditions is—
-- src:2291 | (a) that a person on whom a requirement has been imposed under regulation 66 has failed (wholly or in part) to comply with it, and
-- src:2292 | (b) that on the premises specified in the warrant—
-- src:2293 | (i) there are documents which have been required, or
-- src:2294 | (ii) there is information which has been required.
@ref reg 70(3) (src:2290-2294)
GIVEN `reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the premises specified in the warrant there are documents which have been required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the premises specified in the warrant there is information which has been required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(3) the first set of conditions is satisfied` IS
    IF `reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66` AND (`on the premises specified in the warrant there are documents which have been required` OR `on the premises specified in the warrant there is information which has been required`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first set of conditions is—" [marginal (a)]

-- src:2295 | (4) The second set of conditions is—
-- src:2296 | (a) that the premises specified in the warrant are premises of—
-- src:2297 | (i) the relevant person or the payment service provider (“P”),
-- src:2298 | (ii) a member of the same group as P; or
-- src:2299 | (iii) a third person referred to in regulation 66(8);
-- src:2300 | (b) that there are on the premises documents or information in relation to which a requirement could be imposed under regulation 66, and
-- src:2301 | (c) that if such a requirement were to be imposed—
-- src:2302 | (i) it would not be complied with, or
-- src:2303 | (ii) the documents or information to which it related would be removed, tampered with or destroyed.
@ref reg 70(4) (src:2295-2303)
GIVEN `the premises specified in the warrant are premises of the relevant person or the payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises specified in the warrant are premises of a member of the same group as that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises specified in the warrant are premises of a third person referred to in regulation 66(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are on the premises documents or information in relation to which a requirement could be imposed under regulation 66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if such a requirement were to be imposed it would not be complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if such a requirement were to be imposed the documents or information to which it related would be removed, tampered with or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(4) the second set of conditions is satisfied` IS
    IF (`the premises specified in the warrant are premises of the relevant person or the payment service provider` OR `the premises specified in the warrant are premises of a member of the same group as that person` OR `the premises specified in the warrant are premises of a third person referred to in regulation 66(8)`) AND `there are on the premises documents or information in relation to which a requirement could be imposed under regulation 66` AND (`if such a requirement were to be imposed it would not be complied with` OR `if such a requirement were to be imposed the documents or information to which it related would be removed, tampered with or destroyed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second set of conditions is—" [marginal (a)]

-- src:2304 | (5) The third set of conditions is—
-- src:2305 | (a) that an officer has been obstructed in the exercise of the power under regulation 69; and
-- src:2306 | (b) that there is on the premises specified in the warrant documents, information or cash which could be inspected under regulation 69(2)(d) or (f).
@ref reg 70(5) (src:2304-2306)
GIVEN `an officer has been obstructed in the exercise of the power under regulation 69` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is on the premises specified in the warrant documents, information or cash which could be inspected under regulation 69(2)(d) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(5) the third set of conditions is satisfied` IS
    IF `an officer has been obstructed in the exercise of the power under regulation 69` AND `there is on the premises specified in the warrant documents, information or cash which could be inspected under regulation 69(2)(d) or (f)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third set of conditions is—" [marginal (a)]

-- src:2307 | (6) The fourth set of conditions is—
-- src:2308 | (a) that an offence under these Regulations has been, is being or is about to be committed by P; and
-- src:2309 | (b) there is on the premises specified in the warrant information or documents relevant to whether the offence has been, is being or is about to be committed.
@ref reg 70(6) (src:2307-2309)
GIVEN `an offence under these Regulations has been, is being or is about to be committed by the relevant person or the payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is on the premises specified in the warrant information or documents relevant to whether the offence has been, is being or is about to be committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(6) the fourth set of conditions is satisfied` IS
    IF `an offence under these Regulations has been, is being or is about to be committed by the relevant person or the payment service provider` AND `there is on the premises specified in the warrant information or documents relevant to whether the offence has been, is being or is about to be committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth set of conditions is—" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 70(7): what a warrant authorises the executing officer to do.  The six are listed without "only"; the use of force is limited to "such force as may be reasonably necessary".
-- src:2310 | (7) A warrant under this regulation authorises the executing officer—
-- src:2311 | (a) to enter the premises specified in the warrant;
-- src:2312 | (b) to search the premises and take possession of any documents or information appearing to be documents or information of a kind in respect of which the warrant was issued (“the relevant kind”) or to take, in relation to any such documents or information, any other steps which may appear to be necessary for preserving them or preventing interference with them;
-- src:2313 | (c) to inspect any cash found on the premises;
-- src:2314 | (d) to take copies of, or extracts from, any documents or information appearing to be of the relevant kind;
-- src:2315 | (e) to require any person on the premises to provide an explanation of any document or information appearing to be of the relevant kind or to state where it may be found; and
-- src:2316 | (f) to use such force as may be reasonably necessary.
@ref reg 70(7) (src:2310-2316)
DECLARE `reg 70(7) authority` IS ONE OF
    `reg 70(7)(a) to enter the premises specified in the warrant`
    `reg 70(7)(b) to search the premises and take possession of documents or information of the relevant kind, or take any other steps necessary for preserving them or preventing interference with them`
    `reg 70(7)(c) to inspect any cash found on the premises`
    `reg 70(7)(d) to take copies of, or extracts from, documents or information of the relevant kind`
    `reg 70(7)(e) to require any person on the premises to provide an explanation of any document or information of the relevant kind or to state where it may be found`
    `reg 70(7)(f) to use such force as may be reasonably necessary`
    `reg 70(7) some other authority`

@ref reg 70(7) (src:2310-2316)
GIVEN `a warrant under this regulation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force used is no more than is reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      authority IS A `reg 70(7) authority`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(7) the warrant authorises the executing officer` IS
    IF `a warrant under this regulation has been issued`
    THEN CONSIDER authority
         WHEN `reg 70(7)(a) to enter the premises specified in the warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(7)(b) to search the premises and take possession of documents or information of the relevant kind, or take any other steps necessary for preserving them or preventing interference with them` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(7)(c) to inspect any cash found on the premises` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(7)(d) to take copies of, or extracts from, documents or information of the relevant kind` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(7)(e) to require any person on the premises to provide an explanation of any document or information of the relevant kind or to state where it may be found` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(7)(f) to use such force as may be reasonably necessary` THEN
             IF `the force used is no more than is reasonably necessary`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such force as may be reasonably necessary"
         WHEN `reg 70(7) some other authority` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): six authorities are listed and the paragraph does not say others are barred
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant under this regulation authorises"

-- Reg 70(8): information held on a computer or in non-legible form.  "Where" is the condition: outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (ruled 2026-11-05, (b)).
-- src:2317 | (8) Where information of the relevant kind is contained in a computer or other storage device, or is recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form, the warrant authorises the executing officer to take possession of that information in a form in which it can be taken away and in which it is legible.
@ref reg 70(8) (src:2317)
GIVEN `a warrant under this regulation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information of the relevant kind is contained in a computer or other storage device, or is recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(8) the warrant authorises the executing officer to take possession of the information in legible form` IS
    IF `a warrant under this regulation has been issued`
    THEN IF `information of the relevant kind is contained in a computer or other storage device, or is recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where information of the relevant kind is contained in a computer or other storage device, or is recorded in any other way otherwise than in legible form, the warrant authorises the executing officer to take possession of that information in a form in which it can be taken away and in which it is visible and legible" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the warrant" is a warrant under this regulation; with none issued the paragraph is not in play (ruled 2026-11-05, (c))

-- Reg 70(9): three features a warrant may have.
-- src:2318 | (9) A warrant under this regulation—
-- src:2319 | (a) may be exercised by any executing officer;
-- src:2320 | (b) may authorise persons to accompany any executing officer who is executing it;
-- src:2321 | (c) may be issued subject to conditions.
@ref reg 70(9) (src:2318-2321)
DECLARE `reg 70(9) feature` IS ONE OF
    `reg 70(9)(a) the warrant may be exercised by any executing officer`
    `reg 70(9)(b) the warrant may authorise persons to accompany any executing officer who is executing it`
    `reg 70(9)(c) the warrant may be issued subject to conditions`
    `reg 70(9) some other feature`

@ref reg 70(9) (src:2318-2321)
GIVEN `a warrant under this regulation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      feature IS A `reg 70(9) feature`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(9) a warrant may have the feature` IS
    IF `a warrant under this regulation has been issued`
    THEN CONSIDER feature
         WHEN `reg 70(9)(a) the warrant may be exercised by any executing officer` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(9)(b) the warrant may authorise persons to accompany any executing officer who is executing it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(9)(c) the warrant may be issued subject to conditions` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 70(9) some other feature` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): three features are listed and the paragraph does not say others are barred
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant under this regulation"

-- Reg 70(10): a person authorised to accompany may exercise the powers in paragraph (7) only in the company of, and under the supervision of, an executing officer.
-- src:2322 | (10) The powers in paragraph (7) may be exercised by a person authorised by the warrant to accompany an executing officer; but that person may exercise those powers only in the company of, and under the supervision of, an executing officer.
@ref reg 70(10) (src:2322)
GIVEN `the person is authorised by the warrant to accompany an executing officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in the company of, and under the supervision of, an executing officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(10) the accompanying person may exercise the powers in paragraph (7)` IS
    IF `the person is authorised by the warrant to accompany an executing officer`
    THEN IF `the person acts in the company of, and under the supervision of, an executing officer`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person may exercise those powers only in the company of, and under the supervision of, an executing officer" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person authorised by the warrant to accompany an executing officer"

-- Reg 70(11) and (12): the safeguards of the Police and Criminal Evidence Act 1984 apply in England and Wales, and the corresponding Articles of the Northern Ireland Order of 1989 in Northern Ireland.  The content of those provisions is outside the sources; the answer says whether they apply.
-- src:2323 | (11) In England and Wales, sections 15(5) to (8) and 16(3) to (12) of the Police and Criminal Evidence Act 1984 (execution of warrants and safeguards) apply to warrants issued under this regulation.
@ref reg 70(11) (src:2323)
GIVEN `where the warrant is issued` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(11) sections 15(5) to (8) and 16(3) to (12) of the Police and Criminal Evidence Act 1984 apply to the warrant` IS
    IF `where the warrant is issued` EQUALS `England and Wales`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In England and Wales"

-- src:2324 | (12) In Northern Ireland, Articles 17(5) to (8) and 18(3) to (12) of the Police and Criminal Evidence (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (execution of warrants and safeguards) apply to warrants issued under this regulation.
@ref reg 70(12) (src:2324)
GIVEN `where the warrant is issued` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(12) Articles 17(5) to (8) and 18(3) to (12) of the Police and Criminal Evidence (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 apply to the warrant` IS
    IF `where the warrant is issued` EQUALS `Northern Ireland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In Northern Ireland"

§§ `Regulation 71 -- Retention of documents taken under regulation 66 or 70`

-- Reg 71(1): seized material may be retained for so long as it is necessary to retain it (rather than copies).
-- src:2337 | (1) Any material possession of which is taken in accordance with a requirement under regulation 66 or under a warrant issued under regulation 70 (“seized material”) may be retained for so long as it is necessary to retain it (rather than copies of it) in connection with the exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority under these Regulations for the purposes of which any requirement was imposed or the warrant was issued.
@ref reg 71(1) (src:2337)
GIVEN `possession of the material was taken in accordance with a requirement under regulation 66 or under a warrant issued under regulation 70` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary to retain it (rather than copies of it) in connection with the exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority under these Regulations for the purposes of which any requirement was imposed or the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 71(1) the seized material may be retained` IS
    IF `possession of the material was taken in accordance with a requirement under regulation 66 or under a warrant issued under regulation 70`
    THEN IF `it is necessary to retain it (rather than copies of it) in connection with the exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority under these Regulations for the purposes of which any requirement was imposed or the warrant was issued`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be retained for so long as it is necessary to retain it" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any material possession of which is taken in accordance with a requirement under regulation 66 or under a warrant issued under regulation 70"

-- Reg 71(2): where an officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting the two things, the material may be retained until the proceedings are concluded.  "If" is the condition, so a case without the grounds answers JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a)); "until the proceedings are concluded" fixes the end in the text's own words, so once they are concluded the answer is JUST FALSE (ruled 2026-11-05, (a)).
-- src:2338 | (2) If a duly authorised officer (within the meaning of regulation 70(13)) has reasonable grounds for suspecting that—
-- src:2339 | (a) the seized material may need to be produced for the purposes of legal proceedings; and
-- src:2340 | (b) it might otherwise be unavailable for those purposes,
-- src:2341 | it may be retained until the proceedings are concluded.
@ref reg 71(2) (src:2338-2341)
GIVEN `reg 70(13) the person is a duly authorised officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that the seized material may need to be produced for the purposes of legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that it might otherwise be unavailable for those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 71(2) the seized material may be retained until the proceedings are concluded` IS
    IF     `reg 70(13) the person is a duly authorised officer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        OR (NOT `the officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that the seized material may need to be produced for the purposes of legal proceedings`)
        OR (NOT `the officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that it might otherwise be unavailable for those purposes`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a duly authorised officer (within the meaning of regulation 70(13)) has reasonable grounds for suspecting" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE IF `reg 70(13) the person is a duly authorised officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN IF NOT `the proceedings are concluded`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it may be retained until the proceedings are concluded" [ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a duly authorised officer is not shown

-- Reg 71(3): a person claiming to be the owner of seized material may apply to the Crown Court or, in Scotland, the sheriff or the summary sheriff for an order for delivery to the person appearing to the court to be the owner.
-- src:2342 | (3) A person claiming to be the owner of any seized material may apply to the Crown Court or (in Scotland) the sheriff or the summary sheriff for an order for the delivery of the material to the person appearing to the court, the sheriff or the summary sheriff to be the owner.
@ref reg 71(3) (src:2342)
DECLARE `reg 71(3) court` IS ONE OF
    `reg 71(3) the Crown Court`
    `reg 71(3) the sheriff or the summary sheriff`

@ref reg 71(3) (src:2342)
GIVEN `the person claims to be the owner of seized material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the application is made` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A MAYBE `reg 71(3) court`
DECIDE `reg 71(3) the person may apply for delivery to` IS
    IF `the person claims to be the owner of seized material`
    THEN IF `where the application is made` EQUALS Scotland
         THEN JUST `reg 71(3) the sheriff or the summary sheriff`
         ELSE JUST `reg 71(3) the Crown Court`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person claiming to be the owner of any seized material"

-- Reg 71(4): if the court cannot ascertain who is the owner it may make such order as it thinks fit.  "If" is the condition: outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2343 | (4) If on an application under paragraph (3), the court or (in Scotland) the sheriff or the summary sheriff cannot ascertain who is the owner of the seized material the court, the sheriff or the summary sheriff may make such order as the court, the sheriff or the summary sheriff thinks fit.
@ref reg 71(4) (src:2343)
GIVEN `an application was made under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court, or in Scotland the sheriff or the summary sheriff, cannot ascertain who is the owner of the seized material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 71(4) the court may make such order as it thinks fit` IS
    IF `an application was made under paragraph (3)` AND `the court, or in Scotland the sheriff or the summary sheriff, cannot ascertain who is the owner of the seized material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under paragraph (3), the court or (in Scotland) the sheriff or the summary sheriff cannot ascertain who is the owner of the seized material the court, the sheriff or the summary sheriff may make such order as the court, sheriff or summary sheriff thinks fit" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 71(5): an order under paragraph (3) or (4) does not affect the right to take legal proceedings for recovery.
-- src:2344 | (5) An order under paragraph (3) or (4) does not affect the right of any person to take legal proceedings against any person in possession of seized material for the recovery of the material.
@ref reg 71(5) (src:2344)
GIVEN `an order was made under paragraph (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 71(5) the order affects the right to take legal proceedings against the person in possession for the recovery of the material` IS
    IF `an order was made under paragraph (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the right of any person to take legal proceedings against any person in possession of seized material for the recovery of the material" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order under paragraph (3) or (4)"

§§ `Regulation 72 -- Provision of information and warrants: safeguards`

-- Reg 72(7): "excluded material".
-- src:2356 | (7) For the purposes of this regulation, “excluded material” means personal records which a person has acquired or created in the course of any trade, business, profession or other occupation or for the purposes of any paid or unpaid office and which is held subject—
-- src:2357 | (a) to an express or implied undertaking to hold it in confidence; or
-- src:2358 | (b) to a restriction on disclosure or an obligation of secrecy contained in any enactment, including an enactment contained in, or made under, an Act passed after this Regulation.
@ref reg 72(7) (src:2356-2358)
GIVEN `the material is personal records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has acquired or created them in the course of any trade, business, profession or other occupation or for the purposes of any paid or unpaid office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are held subject to an express or implied undertaking to hold them in confidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are held subject to a restriction on disclosure or an obligation of secrecy contained in any enactment, including an enactment contained in, or made under, an Act passed after this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(7) the material is excluded material` IS
    IF `the material is personal records` AND `a person has acquired or created them in the course of any trade, business, profession or other occupation or for the purposes of any paid or unpaid office` AND (`they are held subject to an express or implied undertaking to hold them in confidence` OR `they are held subject to a restriction on disclosure or an obligation of secrecy contained in any enactment, including an enactment contained in, or made under, an Act passed after this Regulation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“excluded material” means personal records which a person has acquired or created"

-- Reg 72(5): "privileged material".  An "is" definition, read as closed (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:2350 | (5) Privileged material is any material which the person would be entitled to refuse to produce on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court.
@ref reg 72(5) (src:2350)
GIVEN `the person would be entitled to refuse to produce the material on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(5) the material is privileged material` IS
    IF `the person would be entitled to refuse to produce the material on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Privileged material is any material which the person would be entitled to refuse to produce on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 72(6): in Scotland the High Court is the Court of Session and the entitlement is one on the grounds of confidentiality of communication.
-- src:2351 | (6) In the application of this regulation to Scotland, the references in paragraphs (1) and (5)—
-- src:2352 | (a) to proceedings in the High Court are to be read as references to proceedings in the Court of Session; and
-- src:2353 | (b) to an entitlement on grounds of legal professional privilege are to be read as references to an entitlement on the grounds of confidentiality of communication—
-- src:2354 | (i) between professional legal advisers and their clients; or
-- src:2355 | (ii) made in connection with or in contemplation of legal proceedings and for the purposes of those proceedings.
@ref reg 72(6) (src:2351-2355)
DECLARE `reg 72(6) court` IS ONE OF
    `reg 72(6)(a) the High Court`
    `reg 72(6)(a) the Court of Session`

@ref reg 72(6)(a) (src:2351-2352)
GIVEN `where this regulation is applied` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A `reg 72(6) court`
DECIDE `reg 72(6)(a) the court whose proceedings are referred to in paragraphs (1) and (5)` IS
    IF `where this regulation is applied` EQUALS Scotland
    THEN `reg 72(6)(a) the Court of Session`
    ELSE `reg 72(6)(a) the High Court`

@ref reg 72(6)(b) (src:2351) (src:2353-2355)
GIVEN `where this regulation is applied` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the communication is between professional legal advisers and their clients` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is made in connection with or in contemplation of legal proceedings and for the purposes of those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(6)(b) the person is entitled to refuse on the grounds of confidentiality of communication` IS
    IF `where this regulation is applied` EQUALS Scotland
    THEN IF `the communication is between professional legal advisers and their clients` OR `the communication is made in connection with or in contemplation of legal proceedings and for the purposes of those proceedings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to an entitlement on the grounds of confidentiality of communication— (i) between professional legal advisers and their clients; or (ii) made in connection with or in contemplation of legal proceedings" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the application of this regulation to Scotland"

-- Reg 72(1): the bar on being required to produce excluded material or privileged information, with the lawyer's exception.  The exception is applied to the privilege limb only (fork F-72-1).
-- src:2346 | (1) A person may not be required under regulation 66, 69 , 70, 74A or 74B to produce excluded material, or to provide information, produce documents or answer questions which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide, produce or answer on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court, except that a lawyer may be required to provide the full name and address of the lawyer's client.
@ref reg 72(1) (src:2346)
GIVEN `the requirement is made under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to produce excluded material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to provide information, produce documents or answer questions which the person would be entitled to refuse to provide, produce or answer on grounds of legal professional privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to provide the full name and address of the lawyer's client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(1) the person may be required` IS
    IF NOT `the requirement is made under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B"
    ELSE IF `it is to produce excluded material`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not be required under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B to produce excluded material" [marginal (a)]
         ELSE IF `it is to provide information, produce documents or answer questions which the person would be entitled to refuse to provide, produce or answer on grounds of legal professional privilege`
              THEN IF `the person is a lawyer` AND `it is to provide the full name and address of the lawyer's client`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or to provide information, produce documents or answer questions which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide, produce or answer on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court" [marginal (a)]
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (1) bars two kinds of requirement and says nothing of any other

-- Reg 72(2): providing information in accordance with these regulations is not a breach of a restriction on disclosure.
-- src:2347 | (2) The provision of information in accordance with regulation 66, 69 , 70, 74A or 74B, is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 72(2) (src:2347)
GIVEN `the information is provided in accordance with regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(2) providing the information breaches a restriction on the disclosure of information` IS
    IF `the information is provided in accordance with regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B"

-- Reg 72(3): no civil liability for a disclosure made in good faith in accordance with these regulations.
-- src:2348 | (3) Where a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with regulations 66, 69 , 70, 74A or 74B no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person making the disclosure.
@ref reg 72(3) (src:2348)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in accordance with regulations 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(3) civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure` IS
    IF `the disclosure is made in good faith` AND `the disclosure is made in accordance with regulations 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person making the disclosure" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with regulations 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B"

-- Reg 72(4): a warrant does not confer the right to seize privileged or excluded material.
-- src:2349 | (4) A warrant issued under regulation 70 does not confer the right to seize privileged material or excluded material.
@ref reg 72(4) (src:2349)
GIVEN `the warrant is issued under regulation 70` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material is privileged material or excluded material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(4) the warrant confers the right to seize the material` IS
    IF `the warrant is issued under regulation 70` AND `the material is privileged material or excluded material`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not confer the right to seize privileged material or excluded material" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant issued under regulation 70"

§§ `Regulation 73 -- Admissibility of statements`

-- Reg 73(1): a statement made in response to one of four requirements may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings.
-- src:2360 | (1) A statement made by a person in response to a requirement imposed under regulations 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e) , 70(7)(e) or 74B(6) may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings.
@ref reg 73(1) (src:2360)
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement imposed under regulation 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sought to use the statement in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 73(1) the statement may be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings` IS
    IF `the statement was made in response to a requirement imposed under regulation 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)` AND `it is sought to use the statement in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person in response to a requirement imposed under regulations 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)"

-- Reg 73(2): where paragraph (1) does not apply.  The six cases are listed without "only".
-- src:2361 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply—
-- src:2362 | (a) in the case of proceedings under Parts 2 to 4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (confiscation proceedings) ;
-- src:2363 | (b) on a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911 (false statements) ;
-- src:2364 | (c) on a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (false statements) ;
-- src:2365 | (d) on a prosecution for an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995 (false statements and declarations) ;
-- src:2366 | (e) on a prosecution for an offence under regulation 88; or
-- src:2367 | (f) for some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1).
@ref reg 73(2) (src:2361-2367)
DECLARE `reg 73(2) case` IS ONE OF
    `reg 73(2)(a) proceedings under Parts 2 to 4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (confiscation proceedings)`
    `reg 73(2)(b) a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911 (false statements)`
    `reg 73(2)(c) a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (false statements)`
    `reg 73(2)(d) a prosecution for an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995 (false statements and declarations)`
    `reg 73(2)(e) a prosecution for an offence under regulation 88`
    `reg 73(2)(f) some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1)`
    `reg 73(2) none of these cases`

@ref reg 73(2) (src:2361-2367)
GIVEN case IS A `reg 73(2) case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 73(2) paragraph (1) applies` IS
    CONSIDER case
    WHEN `reg 73(2)(a) proceedings under Parts 2 to 4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (confiscation proceedings)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply— (a) in the case of proceedings under Parts 2 to 4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 73(2)(b) a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911 (false statements)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply— (b) on a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 73(2)(c) a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (false statements)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply— (c) on a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 73(2)(d) a prosecution for an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995 (false statements and declarations)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply— (d) on a prosecution for an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 73(2)(e) a prosecution for an offence under regulation 88` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply— (e) on a prosecution for an offence under regulation 88" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 73(2)(f) some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply— (f) for some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1)" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 73(2) none of these cases` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): six cases are listed and the paragraph does not say that paragraph (1) applies in every other

-- Reg 73(3): a statement may not be used by virtue of paragraph (2)(f) unless evidence relating to it is adduced or a question relating to it is asked, by the person or on their behalf, in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution.
-- src:2368 | (3) A statement may not be used by virtue of paragraph (2)(f) against a person unless—
-- src:2369 | (a) evidence relating to it is adduced; or
-- src:2370 | (b) a question relating to it is asked;
-- src:2371 | by them or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution.
@ref reg 73(3) (src:2368-2371)
GIVEN `it is sought to use the statement against the person by virtue of paragraph (2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `evidence relating to it is adduced by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question relating to it is asked by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 73(3) the statement may be used by virtue of paragraph (2)(f)` IS
    IF `it is sought to use the statement against the person by virtue of paragraph (2)(f)`
    THEN IF `evidence relating to it is adduced by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` OR `a question relating to it is asked by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement may not be used by virtue of paragraph (2)(f) against a person unless" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by virtue of paragraph (2)(f)"

-- Reg 73 as a whole (hand-gathered, ruling E1 option B as guidance): is the statement protected from use against the person?  Paragraphs (1), (2) and (3) each keep their own function.  JUST TRUE: protected.  JUST FALSE: an exception takes it outside paragraph (1), or paragraph (3) lets it in.  NOTHING: the statement was not made in response to one of the four requirements, which the regulation does not address.
-- src:2360 | (1) A statement made by a person in response to a requirement imposed under regulations 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e) , 70(7)(e) or 74B(6) may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings.
-- src:2361 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply—
-- src:2362 | (a) in the case of proceedings under Parts 2 to 4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (confiscation proceedings) ;
-- src:2363 | (b) on a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911 (false statements) ;
-- src:2364 | (c) on a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (false statements) ;
-- src:2365 | (d) on a prosecution for an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995 (false statements and declarations) ;
-- src:2366 | (e) on a prosecution for an offence under regulation 88; or
-- src:2367 | (f) for some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1).
-- src:2368 | (3) A statement may not be used by virtue of paragraph (2)(f) against a person unless—
-- src:2369 | (a) evidence relating to it is adduced; or
-- src:2370 | (b) a question relating to it is asked;
-- src:2371 | by them or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution.
@ref reg 73(1) to (3) (src:2360-2371)
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement imposed under regulation 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      case IS A `reg 73(2) case`
      `evidence relating to the statement is adduced, or a question relating to it is asked, by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 73 the statement is protected from use in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings` IS
    IF NOT `the statement was made in response to a requirement imposed under regulation 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person in response to a requirement imposed under regulations 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)"
    ELSE IF `reg 73(2) paragraph (1) applies` case EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF case EQUALS `reg 73(2)(f) some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in paragraph (1)`
              THEN IF `evidence relating to the statement is adduced, or a question relating to it is asked, by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution`
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply— (f)" with paragraph (3) satisfied [marginal (a)]
                   ELSE JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply—" [marginal (a)]

§§ `Regulation 74 -- Powers of relevant officers`

-- Reg 74(1): a relevant officer may only exercise powers under this Part pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or the Commissioners by or on behalf of its authority or the Department for the Economy.
-- src:2373 | (1) A relevant officer (“R”) may only exercise powers under this Part pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners—
-- src:2374 | (a) by or on behalf of the local weights and measures authority of which R is an officer (“R's authority”); or
-- src:2375 | (b) by the Department for the Economy.
@ref reg 74(1) (src:2373-2375)
GIVEN `reg 65(2) the person is a relevant officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `R acts pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements are made by or on behalf of the local weights and measures authority of which R is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements are made by the Department for the Economy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74(1) R may exercise powers under this Part` IS
    IF `reg 65(2) the person is a relevant officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `R acts pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners` AND (`the arrangements are made by or on behalf of the local weights and measures authority of which R is an officer` OR `the arrangements are made by the Department for the Economy`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only exercise powers under this Part pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA or with the Commissioners" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant officer is not shown

-- Reg 74(2): what a relevant officer does is treated as done by an officer of the FCA, or of Revenue and Customs, according to the arrangements.
-- src:2376 | (2) Anything done or omitted to be done by, or in relation to, R in the exercise or purported exercise of a power in this Part is to be treated for all purposes as having been done or omitted to be done by, or in relation to—
-- src:2377 | (a) an officer of the FCA, if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA, or
-- src:2378 | (b) an officer of Revenue and Customs, if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners.
@ref reg 74(2) (src:2376-2378)
GIVEN `the thing was done or omitted to be done by, or in relation to, R in the exercise or purported exercise of a power in this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74(2)(a) anything done by R is treated as done by an officer of the FCA` IS
    IF `the thing was done or omitted to be done by, or in relation to, R in the exercise or purported exercise of a power in this Part` AND `R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to be treated for all purposes as having been done or omitted to be done by, or in relation to— (a) an officer of the FCA, if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA" [marginal (a)]

@ref reg 74(2)(b) (src:2378)
GIVEN `the thing was done or omitted to be done by, or in relation to, R in the exercise or purported exercise of a power in this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74(2)(b) anything done by R is treated as done by an officer of Revenue and Customs` IS
    IF `the thing was done or omitted to be done by, or in relation to, R in the exercise or purported exercise of a power in this Part` AND `R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or (b) an officer of Revenue and Customs, if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 74(3): paragraph (2) does not apply for the purpose of criminal proceedings against R, R's authority, the Department, the FCA or the Commissioners.
-- src:2379 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply for the purpose of any criminal proceedings brought against R, R's authority, the Department for the Economy, the FCA or the Commissioners, in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by R.
@ref reg 74(3) (src:2379)
GIVEN `criminal proceedings are brought against R, R's authority, the Department for the Economy, the FCA or the Commissioners, in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by R` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74(3) paragraph (2) applies` IS
    IF `criminal proceedings are brought against R, R's authority, the Department for the Economy, the FCA or the Commissioners, in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by R`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) does not apply for the purpose of any criminal proceedings" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says when paragraph (2) does not apply and nothing of when it does

-- Reg 74(4): R must not disclose information obtained in the exercise of such powers to any person other than the four named, unless R has approval or is under a duty.  JUST TRUE: the prohibition applies to this disclosure.
-- src:2380 | (4) R must not disclose to any person other than the FCA (if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA), the Commissioners (if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners), R's authority or, as the case may be, the Department of the Economy, information obtained by R in the exercise of such powers unless—
-- src:2381 | (a) R has the approval of the FCA or where appropriate the Commissioners to do so, or
-- src:2382 | (b) R is under a duty to make the disclosure.
@ref reg 74(4) (src:2380-2382)
GIVEN `the information was obtained by R in the exercise of such powers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is the FCA and R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is the Commissioners and R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is R's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is the Department for the Economy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `R has the approval of the FCA or where appropriate the Commissioners to make the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `R is under a duty to make the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74(4) R must not disclose the information` IS
    IF NOT `the information was obtained by R in the exercise of such powers`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information obtained by R in the exercise of such powers"
    ELSE IF     `the recipient is the FCA and R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA`
             OR `the recipient is the Commissioners and R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners`
             OR `the recipient is R's authority`
             OR `the recipient is the Department for the Economy`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to any person other than the FCA (if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the FCA), the Commissioners (if R is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners), R's authority or, as the case may be, the Department of the Economy" [marginal (a)]
         ELSE IF `R has the approval of the FCA or where appropriate the Commissioners to make the disclosure` OR `R is under a duty to make the disclosure`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— (a) R has the approval of the FCA or where appropriate the Commissioners to do so, or (b) R is under a duty to make the disclosure" [marginal (a)]
              ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Regulation 74A -- Reporting requirements: cryptoasset businesses`

-- Reg 74A(1): each cryptoasset exchange provider and custodian wallet provider must provide to the FCA such information as the FCA may direct, under one of three heads.  A business can be several kinds at once, so the kinds are a list of the core's type.
-- src:2384 | (1) Each cryptoasset exchange provider and custodian wallet provider (“cryptoasset business”) must provide to the FCA such information as the FCA may direct—
-- src:2385 | (a) about compliance by the cryptoasset business with requirements imposed in or under Parts 2 to 6 and 7A of these Regulations;
-- src:2386 | (b) which is required by the FCA for the purpose of calculating charges under regulation 102 (costs of supervision); or
-- src:2387 | (c) which is otherwise reasonably required by the FCA in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its supervisory functions.
@ref reg 74A(1) (src:2384-2387)
GIVEN `the kinds of relevant person the business is` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `the FCA has directed the business to provide the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is about compliance by the cryptoasset business with requirements imposed in or under Parts 2 to 6 and 7A of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is required by the FCA for the purpose of calculating charges under regulation 102 (costs of supervision)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is otherwise reasonably required by the FCA in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74A(1) the cryptoasset business must provide the information to the FCA` IS
    IF (elem `cryptoasset exchange provider` `the kinds of relevant person the business is` OR elem `custodian wallet provider` `the kinds of relevant person the business is`) AND `the FCA has directed the business to provide the information` AND (`the information is about compliance by the cryptoasset business with requirements imposed in or under Parts 2 to 6 and 7A of these Regulations` OR `the information is required by the FCA for the purpose of calculating charges under regulation 102 (costs of supervision)` OR `the information is otherwise reasonably required by the FCA in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its supervisory functions`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Each cryptoasset exchange provider and custodian wallet provider ... such information as the FCA may direct" under one of the three heads

-- Reg 74A(2): the time, form and verification are as the FCA directs.  A point on which the FCA gave no direction is not covered.
-- src:2388 | (2) The information referred to in paragraph (1) must be provided at such times and in such form, and verified in such manner, as the FCA may direct.
@ref reg 74A(2) (src:2388)
GIVEN `the information was provided at the times the FCA directed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information was provided in the form the FCA directed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information was verified in the manner the FCA directed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74A(2) the information was provided as the FCA directed` IS
    IF     `the information was provided at the times the FCA directed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        OR `the information was provided in the form the FCA directed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        OR `the information was verified in the manner the FCA directed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be provided at such times and in such form, and verified in such manner, as the FCA may direct" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE IF     `the information was provided at the times the FCA directed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR `the information was provided in the form the FCA directed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR `the information was verified in the manner the FCA directed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the FCA gave no direction on time, form or verification

§§ `Regulation 74B -- Report by a skilled person: cryptoasset businesses`

-- Reg 74B(1): when the regulation applies.  The FCA's belief must be reasonable; that is a judgment the text hands to the FCA, taken as an input.  "Applies where": the whole of the where clause is the condition, including that the relevant person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (ruled 2026-11-05, (b)).
-- src:2390 | (1) This regulation applies where the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person, concerning a matter relating to the exercise of the FCA’s functions under these Regulations, is required in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its functions under these Regulations in relation to a relevant person who is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider.
@ref reg 74B(1) (src:2390)
GIVEN `the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person, concerning a matter relating to the exercise of the FCA's functions under these Regulations, is required in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its functions under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kinds of relevant person the relevant person is` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74B(1) this regulation applies` IS
    IF `the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person, concerning a matter relating to the exercise of the FCA's functions under these Regulations, is required in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its functions under these Regulations` AND (elem `cryptoasset exchange provider` `the kinds of relevant person the relevant person is` OR elem `custodian wallet provider` `the kinds of relevant person the relevant person is`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies where the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person ... is required ... in relation to a relevant person who is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]

-- Reg 74B(2): the FCA may either require the relevant person, by notice in writing, to appoint a skilled person, or itself appoint one and recover its expenses as a fee payable by the relevant person.
-- src:2391 | (2) The FCA may either—
-- src:2392 | (a) by notice in writing to the relevant person, require the relevant person to appoint a skilled person to provide the FCA with a report on the matter concerned, or
-- src:2393 | (b) itself appoint a skilled person to do so, and recover any expenses incurred in doing so as a fee to be payable by the relevant person concerned.
@ref reg 74B(2) (src:2391-2393)
DECLARE `reg 74B(2) step` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74B(2)(a) require the relevant person by notice in writing to appoint a skilled person to provide the FCA with a report on the matter concerned`
    `reg 74B(2)(b) itself appoint a skilled person to provide the FCA with a report on the matter concerned`

@ref reg 74B(2) (src:2391-2393)
GIVEN `reg 74B(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the FCA gives notice in writing to the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      step IS A `reg 74B(2) step`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74B(2) the FCA may take the step` IS
    IF `reg 74B(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER step
         WHEN `reg 74B(2)(a) require the relevant person by notice in writing to appoint a skilled person to provide the FCA with a report on the matter concerned` THEN
             IF `the FCA gives notice in writing to the relevant person`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by notice in writing to the relevant person"
         WHEN `reg 74B(2)(b) itself appoint a skilled person to provide the FCA with a report on the matter concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `reg 74B(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies where the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): reg 74B(1) has not been answered

@ref reg 74B(2)(b) fee (src:2393)
GIVEN `the FCA itself appointed the skilled person under paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenses the FCA incurred in doing so, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 74B(2)(b) the fee payable by the relevant person is` IS
    IF `the FCA itself appointed the skilled person under paragraph (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST `the expenses the FCA incurred in doing so, in pounds`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "itself appoint a skilled person to do so, and recover any expenses incurred in doing so as a fee"

-- Reg 74B(3): when acting under paragraph (2)(a), what the FCA may require.  Two are listed without "only".  "When" counts as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05): outside paragraph (2)(a) the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:2394 | (3) When acting under paragraph (2)(a), the FCA may require—
-- src:2395 | (a) the report to be in such form as may be specified in the notice; and
-- src:2396 | (b) that the contract between the skilled person and the relevant person contain certain terms that the FCA considers appropriate.
@ref reg 74B(3) (src:2394-2396)
DECLARE `reg 74B(3) requirement` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74B(3)(a) the report to be in such form as may be specified in the notice`
    `reg 74B(3)(b) that the contract between the skilled person and the relevant person contain certain terms that the FCA considers appropriate`
    `reg 74B(3) some other requirement`

@ref reg 74B(3) (src:2394-2396)
GIVEN `the FCA is acting under paragraph (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      requirement IS A `reg 74B(3) requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74B(3) the FCA may require` IS
    IF `the FCA is acting under paragraph (2)(a)`
    THEN CONSIDER requirement
         WHEN `reg 74B(3)(a) the report to be in such form as may be specified in the notice` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 74B(3)(b) that the contract between the skilled person and the relevant person contain certain terms that the FCA considers appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 74B(3) some other requirement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): two requirements are listed and the paragraph does not say others are barred
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When acting under paragraph (2)(a), the FCA may require—" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where (read from "when")]

-- Reg 74B(4): the FCA must give notice in writing of an appointment under paragraph (2)(b) to the relevant person.
-- src:2397 | (4) The FCA must give notice in writing of an appointment under paragraph (2)(b) to the relevant person.
@ref reg 74B(4) (src:2397)
GIVEN `the FCA made an appointment under paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA gave notice in writing of the appointment to the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74B(4) the FCA gave notice in writing of the appointment` IS
    IF `the FCA made an appointment under paragraph (2)(b)`
    THEN IF `the FCA gave notice in writing of the appointment to the relevant person`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The FCA must give notice in writing of an appointment under paragraph (2)(b) to the relevant person" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an appointment under paragraph (2)(b)"

-- Reg 74B(5): who is a "skilled person".
-- src:2398 | (5) References in this regulation to a skilled person are to a person—
-- src:2399 | (a) appearing to the FCA to have the skills necessary to make a report on the matter concerned, and
-- src:2400 | (b) where the appointment is to be made by the relevant person, nominated or approved by the FCA.
@ref reg 74B(5) (src:2398-2400)
GIVEN `the person appears to the FCA to have the skills necessary to make a report on the matter concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is to be made by the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is nominated or approved by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74B(5) the person is a skilled person` IS
    IF `the person appears to the FCA to have the skills necessary to make a report on the matter concerned` AND ((NOT `the appointment is to be made by the relevant person`) OR `the person is nominated or approved by the FCA`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this regulation to a skilled person are to a person— (a) appearing to the FCA to have the skills necessary to make a report on the matter concerned, and (b) where the appointment is to be made by the relevant person, nominated or approved by the FCA" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 74B(6): the duty of the relevant person and any connected person to assist the skilled person.
-- src:2401 | (6) It is the duty of the relevant person and any connected person to give the skilled person all such assistance as the skilled person may reasonably require.
@ref reg 74B(6) (src:2401)
GIVEN `the person is the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 65(3) the person is a connected person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person gave the skilled person all such assistance as the skilled person may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74B(6) the person gave the skilled person the assistance` IS
    IF `the person is the relevant person` OR (`reg 65(3) the person is a connected person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN IF `the person gave the skilled person all such assistance as the skilled person may reasonably require`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is the duty of the relevant person and any connected person to give the skilled person all such assistance as the skilled person may reasonably require" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the relevant person and any connected person"

§§ `Regulation 74C -- Directions: cryptoasset businesses`

-- Reg 74C(1): the FCA may exercise its powers of direction in writing in relation to a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider.
-- src:2403 | (1) The FCA may exercise its powers of direction under paragraph (5) or (6) in writing in relation to a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider (“cryptoasset business”).
@ref reg 74C(1) (src:2403)
GIVEN `the FCA exercises them in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA exercises them under paragraph (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kinds of relevant person the business is` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(1) the FCA may exercise its powers of direction` IS
    IF `the FCA exercises them in writing` AND `the FCA exercises them under paragraph (5) or (6)` AND (elem `cryptoasset exchange provider` `the kinds of relevant person the business is` OR elem `custodian wallet provider` `the kinds of relevant person the business is`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in writing in relation to a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider"

-- Reg 74C(2): a direction may be imposed before, on or after registration.  The three times cover every time, so every answer is yes.
-- src:2404 | (2) A direction may be imposed before, on or after registration, as the FCA considers appropriate.
@ref reg 74C(2) (src:2404)
DECLARE `reg 74C(2) time` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74C(2) before registration`
    `reg 74C(2) on registration`
    `reg 74C(2) after registration`

@ref reg 74C(2) (src:2404)
GIVEN time IS A `reg 74C(2) time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(2) a direction may be imposed at the time` IS
    CONSIDER time
    WHEN `reg 74C(2) before registration` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 74C(2) on registration` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 74C(2) after registration` THEN JUST TRUE

-- Reg 74C(3): the purposes for which a direction may be imposed.  Three are listed without "only".
-- src:2405 | (3) A direction may be imposed for the purpose of—
-- src:2406 | (a) remedying a failure to comply with a requirement under these Regulations;
-- src:2407 | (b) preventing a failure to comply, or continued non-compliance with a requirement under these Regulations;
-- src:2408 | (c) preventing the cryptoasset business from being used for money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing.
@ref reg 74C(3) (src:2405-2408)
DECLARE `reg 74C(3) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74C(3)(a) remedying a failure to comply with a requirement under these Regulations`
    `reg 74C(3)(b) preventing a failure to comply, or continued non-compliance with a requirement under these Regulations`
    `reg 74C(3)(c) preventing the cryptoasset business from being used for money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing`
    `reg 74C(3) some other purpose`

@ref reg 74C(3) (src:2405-2408)
GIVEN purpose IS A `reg 74C(3) purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(3) a direction may be imposed for the purpose` IS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `reg 74C(3)(a) remedying a failure to comply with a requirement under these Regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 74C(3)(b) preventing a failure to comply, or continued non-compliance with a requirement under these Regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 74C(3)(c) preventing the cryptoasset business from being used for money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 74C(3) some other purpose` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): three purposes are listed and the paragraph does not say others are barred

-- Reg 74C(4): a direction may require or prohibit the taking of specified action.
-- src:2409 | (4) A direction may require or prohibit the taking of specified action.
@ref reg 74C(4) (src:2409)
DECLARE `reg 74C(4) content` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74C(4) require the taking of specified action`
    `reg 74C(4) prohibit the taking of specified action`
    `reg 74C(4) some other content`

@ref reg 74C(4) (src:2409)
GIVEN content IS A `reg 74C(4) content`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(4) a direction may have the content` IS
    CONSIDER content
    WHEN `reg 74C(4) require the taking of specified action` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 74C(4) prohibit the taking of specified action` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 74C(4) some other content` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may require or prohibit the taking of specified action" does not say that a direction may do nothing else

-- Reg 74C(5) and (6): the FCA's powers on its own initiative and on the business's request.
-- src:2410 | (5) The FCA may, on its own initiative—
-- src:2411 | (a) impose a new direction;
-- src:2412 | (b) vary a direction imposed under this regulation; or
-- src:2413 | (c) rescind such a direction.
@ref reg 74C(5) (src:2410-2413)
DECLARE `reg 74C(5) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74C(5)(a) impose a new direction`
    `reg 74C(5)(b) vary a direction imposed under this regulation`
    `reg 74C(5)(c) rescind such a direction`

@ref reg 74C(5) (src:2410-2413)
GIVEN `the FCA acts on its own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `reg 74C(5) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(5) the FCA may on its own initiative` IS
    IF `the FCA acts on its own initiative`
    THEN CONSIDER act
         WHEN `reg 74C(5)(a) impose a new direction` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 74C(5)(b) vary a direction imposed under this regulation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 74C(5)(c) rescind such a direction` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on its own initiative"

-- src:2414 | (6) The FCA may, on the request of a cryptoasset business—
-- src:2415 | (a) impose a new direction;
-- src:2416 | (b) vary a direction imposed under this regulation; or
-- src:2417 | (c) rescind such a direction.
@ref reg 74C(6) (src:2414-2417)
DECLARE `reg 74C(6) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 74C(6)(a) impose a new direction`
    `reg 74C(6)(b) vary a direction imposed under this regulation`
    `reg 74C(6)(c) rescind such a direction`

@ref reg 74C(6) (src:2414-2417)
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business has requested it` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `reg 74C(6) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(6) the FCA may on the request of the cryptoasset business` IS
    IF `the cryptoasset business has requested it`
    THEN CONSIDER act
         WHEN `reg 74C(6)(a) impose a new direction` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 74C(6)(b) vary a direction imposed under this regulation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 74C(6)(c) rescind such a direction` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the request of a cryptoasset business"

-- Reg 74C(7): the FCA must consult the PRA before imposing or varying a direction that relates to a PRA authorised person or a member of a group that includes one.
-- src:2418 | (7) The FCA must consult the PRA before imposing or varying a direction which relates to—
-- src:2419 | (a) a person who is a PRA authorised person; or
-- src:2420 | (b) a person who is a member of a group which includes a PRA authorised person.
@ref reg 74C(7) (src:2418-2420)
GIVEN `the FCA imposes or varies a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction relates to a PRA authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction relates to a member of a group which includes a PRA authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA consulted the PRA before imposing or varying the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(7) the FCA consulted the PRA as required` IS
    IF `the FCA imposes or varies a direction` AND (`the direction relates to a PRA authorised person` OR `the direction relates to a member of a group which includes a PRA authorised person`)
    THEN IF `the FCA consulted the PRA before imposing or varying the direction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The FCA must consult the PRA before imposing or varying a direction" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a direction which relates to— (a) a person who is a PRA authorised person; or (b) a person who is a member of a group which includes a PRA authorised person"

-- Reg 74C(8): a direction may be expressed to expire, and its expiry does not affect the FCA's power to impose a new direction.
-- src:2421 | (8) A direction may be expressed to expire at the end of such period as the FCA may specify, but the imposition of a direction that expires at the end of a specified period does not affect the FCA’s power to impose a new direction.
@ref reg 74C(8) (src:2421)
GIVEN `the period is one the FCA specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(8) the direction may be expressed to expire at the end of the period` IS
    IF `the period is one the FCA specifies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such period as the FCA may specify"

@ref reg 74C(8) (src:2421)
GIVEN `the direction expires at the end of a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(8) the expiry of the direction affects the FCA's power to impose a new direction` IS
    IF `the direction expires at the end of a specified period`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the FCA's power to impose a new direction" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a direction that expires at the end of a specified period"

-- Reg 74C(9) to (19): the notices the FCA must give, and what they must contain.
-- src:2422 | (9) If the FCA imposes or varies a direction under paragraph (5)(a) or (b) it must give the cryptoasset business a notice in writing.
@ref reg 74C(9) (src:2422)
GIVEN `the FCA imposed or varied a direction under paragraph (5)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74C(9) the duty to give the notice in writing arises` IS
    IF `the FCA imposed or varied a direction under paragraph (5)(a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
